From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caboose <caboose@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/15] Connect the guest encoder to the client device over a
 Unix socket

CABOOSE_GFXSTREAM_SOCKET selects CabooseSocketStream (connection-manager/
SocketStream.cpp, installed from the Caboose repository) instead of the
virtio-gpu, QEMU pipe or address-space transports. Socket mode does not query
VirtGpu capabilities or render control; the hello exchange establishes the wire
features and SetupInstanceForProcess selects them directly.

Host-visible allocations get a guest-owned aligned shadow, and mapped memory is
exchanged with explicit flush/invalidate payloads instead of direct mapping.
The two mapped-memory entry points report a truncated reply as
VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST instead of aborting, and WHOLE_SIZE ranges end at the
guest's mapping. Without CABOOSE_GFXSTREAM_PRIVATE_ICD, setting the socket
variable makes instance creation fail closed.
